# --- generated output (never source; see 3d/CLAUDE.md) ---
3d/out/
3d/d.vtk
3d/tools/_refcache/

# --- ROS 2 colcon workspace ---
ros2/build/
ros2/install/
ros2/log/
ros2/pixi/.pixi/          # the conda env itself: ~2.3 GB, rebuilt by `pixi install`

# --- python ---
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# --- macOS ---
.DS_Store

# --- OrcaSlicer CLI logs into the CWD (tools/slice_orca.py) ---
3d/*.log

# --- terrain seed sweep ---
# MuJoCo caches a heightfield by file name inside a process, so sweeping seeds
# writes one scene + one png per seed.  Scratch: the committed terrain is
# terrain.png / scene_terrain.xml at terrain.SEED.
ros2/smalldog_description/mujoco/sweep_terrain_*.xml
ros2/smalldog_description/meshes/sweep_terrain_*.png

# --- RL ---
# runs/ is checkpoints and rollout video; uv.lock is deliberately NOT here,
# a pinned resolution is the point when three machines share one tree.
rl/runs/
rl/.venv/
# XLA's compiled executables and its per-fusion autotuning, keyed on the HLO and
# the jax/jaxlib versions.  Machine-local by construction, and disposable: see
# rl/jaxenv.py, which has the rm and why there is no size cap.
rl/.jax_cache/

# --- bench ---
# The raw servo logs ARE versioned, as of 2026-09-09. They used to be ignored on
# the grounds that the fit's output (rl/params/st3215.json) was the thing worth
# keeping — that was wrong twice over. The identification set is a measurement of
# a real servo that cannot be retaken once the unit changes, and it is the only
# evidence behind ST3215_STS3215_measured_parameters.md, which tells the public
# the CSVs are in this repository. It is also how a bench result reaches the WSL2
# box and the Pi: no shared filesystem, no scp, the repo is the only thing that
# crosses. 57 runs is 25 MB raw and 4.6 MB packed.
#
# What still does not belong here: anything from a scratch or exploratory session
# that no document cites. Every file under data/ should be a run some analysis
# actually reads — bench/fit_bam.py loads the whole directory, so a junk run is
# not inert, it is a data point.
